{"title":"Number Of Divisible Substrings","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Map letters using the groups `ab` → 1, `cde` → 2, `fgh` → 3, `ijk` → 4, `lmn` → 5, `opq` → 6, `rst` → 7, `uvw` → 8, and `xyz` → 9.\n\nA string is divisible if the sum of the mapped values of its characters is divisible by its length.\nGiven a string s, return the number of divisible substrings of s.\nA substring is a contiguous non-empty sequence of characters within a string.\n \n## Examples\n\n### Example 1:\n\nSubstring\nMapped\nSum\nLength\nDivisible?\n\na\n1\n1\n1\nYes\n\ns\n7\n7\n1\nYes\n\nd\n2\n2\n1\nYes\n\nf\n3\n3\n1\nYes\n\nas\n1, 7\n8\n2\nYes\n\nsd\n7, 2\n9\n2\nNo\n\ndf\n2, 3\n5\n2\nNo\n\nasd\n1, 7, 2\n10\n3\nNo\n\nsdf\n7, 2, 3\n12\n3\nYes\n\nasdf\n1, 7, 2, 3\n13\n4\nNo\n\n```text\nInput: word = \"asdf\"\nOutput: 6\n```\nExplanation: The table above contains the details about every substring of word, and we can see that 6 of them are divisible.\n\n### Example 2:\n\n```text\nInput: word = \"bdh\"\nOutput: 4\n```\nExplanation: The 4 divisible substrings are: \"b\", \"d\", \"h\", \"bdh\".\nIt can be shown that there are no other substrings of word that are divisible.\n\n### Example 3:\n\n```text\nInput: word = \"abcd\"\nOutput: 6\n```\nExplanation: The 6 divisible substrings are: \"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"ab\", \"cd\".\nIt can be shown that there are no other substrings of word that are divisible.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= word.length <= 2000\n- word consists only of lowercase English letters.\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def countDivisibleSubstrings(self, word: str) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().countDivisibleSubstrings","parameters":[{"name":"word","type":"str"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":["aa"],"expected":3},{"input":["aacjivknneuvtwqudtnoljspdowndndjoifm"],"expected":121},{"input":["aatifcbikawjmdmnxkygwzh"],"expected":60},{"input":["acoiumgfxoafafsvbclybvhhpijszlxurkuyw"],"expected":127},{"input":["acwqsiehghjycchocapyeylznmukyoetut